00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.290
In this video, I'm just going to
demonstrate some of the various tools

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.580
that you can utilize within Word to
structure and layout your document.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.510
So there are a wide range of formatting
tools within Word and we will cover

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.400
certain other ones in other videos.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.550
But the ones I'm going to focus on
here are looking at the cut, copy

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.190
and paste and moving text around and
how you can use the sort function

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.080
and the find and replace function.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:29.654
So as you can see, I have an example
letter on the screen in front of me.

00:00:30.044 --> 00:00:32.720
And first thing I'm going to
demonstrate is how you can select text.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:38.430
The first thing to do is you can click
and hold your mouse button and drag your

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.970
cursor along till you've highlighted
the text that you wish to select.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.590
Alternatively, you can, if you want
to select just a single word, you

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.520
can just double click on the word
and it will just select a word.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.780
If you wanted to select a whole
sentence, so rather than dragging

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.970
and hold your mouse button, if you
just click three times, it will

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.920
automatically select that whole sentence.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.090
Similarly if I wanted to select a whole
paragraph, I would just click three times

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.560
and it would select the whole paragraph.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:09.840
So if I had a paragraph that I wish to
move around to another position within

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.530
the document, I could quite simply,
while it's highlighted, I could click

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.250
and hold the mouse button and as you can
see that's allowing me then to move it.

00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:22.215
The cursor's moving down and once I
release the cursor it automatically moves

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:25.105
that text to the bottom of the page.

00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:28.125
And what I'm going to do is I'm
just going to put that back.

00:01:28.155 --> 00:01:32.025
And this brings into play another tool
that you can use, which is the undo tool.

00:01:32.415 --> 00:01:36.825
So if you look on the tool bar
at the very top, and you can see

00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:41.505
there's a little arrow that points
to the left and that's an undo.

00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:45.765
So if I click on that, it will undo what
I've done and place a text back there.

00:01:46.215 --> 00:01:50.325
And again, if I wanted to move it back,
rather than having to do it manually again

00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:52.545
by selecting it and just click the redo.

00:01:53.595 --> 00:01:56.375
Now you can basically go back
as many steps as you want,

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:58.605
until the document was opened.

00:01:58.665 --> 00:02:02.535
So if I had done 20 steps, but I
needed to go back to the beginning, I

00:02:02.535 --> 00:02:04.845
could quickly undo all of those steps.

00:02:05.175 --> 00:02:07.605
So I'm just going to undo
that and move one again there.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.930
So alternatively, to move you can
also cut and copy information.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.570
So if you cut something, it
does exactly what it says.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:20.180
So if I highlight that text there and
then select the scissors that will

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.280
automatically cut that text out of there.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.480
And as you can see, it's left the
full stop, which is why I'm just

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.740
going to pop that back in there.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:33.500
It's sometimes easier to use the select by
clicking three times and I will cut that.

00:02:34.215 --> 00:02:37.225
And then I can then move that
to wherever I want to paste it.

00:02:37.605 --> 00:02:39.075
So that is very similar.

00:02:39.165 --> 00:02:43.515
Exactly the same as the move, you can
cut information from one document or move

00:02:43.515 --> 00:02:46.845
information from one document, place it
somewhere else within the document, or

00:02:46.845 --> 00:02:49.215
even move it to another open document.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:54.075
And again, I'm just going to undo
that by - I'll use the shortcut for

00:02:54.075 --> 00:02:57.195
the undo, which is Control (ctrl)
and Z, so again, that just places

00:02:57.405 --> 00:02:59.085
that back, takes us a step back.

00:02:59.114 --> 00:03:02.324
The alternative to that is I can copy,
but obviously a copy does what it says.

00:03:02.324 --> 00:03:05.984
It copies the information so
I can use the copy tool there.

00:03:06.014 --> 00:03:10.004
Or I can just go Control and C,
now that's copied the information.

00:03:10.094 --> 00:03:14.294
Nothing appears to have happened, but if
I click the cursor further down the screen

00:03:14.354 --> 00:03:19.424
and then select paste, which I'm going
to use the shortcut Control and V, and

00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:21.494
I'll paste that information into there.

00:03:22.244 --> 00:03:26.444
So those are some of the basic tools
in relation to cut, copy paste.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:30.704
And one of the other tools that
I'm going to demonstrate is the

00:03:30.704 --> 00:03:32.144
use of the find and replace.

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:36.794
And as you can see, there is a
word "group" that occurs several

00:03:36.794 --> 00:03:37.964
times within this document.

00:03:37.964 --> 00:03:39.944
And I want to change
that to the word "team".

00:03:40.844 --> 00:03:43.544
Now, as you can imagine, I've only
got one letter here, so I could go

00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:46.874
through and change each instance
of the word "group" with the word

00:03:46.874 --> 00:03:50.024
"team", just by simply highlighting
that and typing the word team.

00:03:51.314 --> 00:03:54.809
Alternatively word has a
feature called find and replace.

00:03:54.809 --> 00:03:59.219
So if you can imagine if I had a document
with 30, 40, 50 pages and I needed a

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:03.599
change every instance of the word "group"
with the word "team", it would take

00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:05.789
quite some time doing it one by one.

00:04:06.089 --> 00:04:09.629
Whereas if I use the find and replace
tool that can be done instantly.

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:13.180
So if I click on the replace
button there, that brings up the

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.860
find and replace dialogue box.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.800
And what I want to do is I want to replace
the word "group" with the word "team".

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:26.515
And as you can see, that's now going
to look for every instance of the

00:04:26.515 --> 00:04:31.075
word "group" with the word "team" so
I can instantly replace all instances.

00:04:31.105 --> 00:04:35.635
So I click on that and it's all
done, we've made 12 replacements.

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:39.445
So if I then look through every
instance of the word "group" has

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.455
been replaced by the word "team".

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:47.050
Alternative to that is I could
- I'll just close out of that and

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.200
just undo what I did - so that's
changed everything back to "group".

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.760
If I go on to replace, again.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.530
There may be instances where
a word that you want to change

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.240
could be part of a bigger word.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.950
So you have to be careful.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:04.130
So it may be a case in that instance you
need to do it one at a time, but again,

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.360
rather than searching through manually
yourself, you can use the find and

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.890
replace tool and so rather than clicking,
replace all, I just click replace.

00:05:11.976 --> 00:05:15.306
It will find every instance of
the word "group" and, then give me

00:05:15.306 --> 00:05:17.326
the option to change it to "team".

00:05:17.766 --> 00:05:21.996
So I click replace and for
every one I'm quite happy.

00:05:22.052 --> 00:05:25.882
That's it, it's finished searching
the document, select OK and that has

00:05:25.882 --> 00:05:29.412
now changed every instance of the
word "group" with the word "team".

00:05:30.522 --> 00:05:34.752
The last thing I'm going to demonstrate is
how you can sort the text alphabetically.

